  "strategy": "1. **Approach and rationale**:\n    *Goal*: Find an improved h for the minimum overlap problem on [0,2] with dx=2/n, integral 1, h[i] in [0,1]\n    *Bottleneck addressed*: Current approach is stuck improving from 0.380870. We need a different global search combined with efficient local refinement\n    *Approach*: We use a hierarchical, adaptive optimization strategy that combines:\n      - Multi-resolution hierarchical optimization (n_levels=4 to 6) for scalability\n      - Randomized restarts from periodic structures\n      - Ascent direction optimization using worst-case gradient\n      - Smoothed objective for derivative-free optimization\n      - Polynomial continuation from coarse levels to fine\n    *Why different*: This approach focuses on explicit exploitation of periodic patterns to reduce worst-case overlaps, unlike previous random or gradient-only exploration\n\n2. **Mathematical specification**:\n    *Variables*: h \u2208 \u211d\u207f with \u2211h = n/2, 0 \u2264 h_i \u2264 1\n    *Objective*: C5 = max_k \u222b| h(x)[1-h(x+k)] dx \u2248  max(np.correlate(h,1-h,mode=\"full\")) * dx\n    *Periodicity approach*:\n      Define h_periodic(x) = g(t) for t = x/(L) - k, L = n/period\n      Requires period divides n dimensionally\n    *Constraints enforcement*:\n      Use exponential transform: let t = exp(\u03bb(t)) / (1+exp(\u03bb(t))) to keep in [0,1]\n      Maintain sum via Lagrange multiplier with projection\n    *Representation*: \n      h_periodic = project_periodic(random_bernoulli, period, L)\n\n3. **Implementation procedure**:\n    *Phases*: adaptive_multi_level(seed, budget)\n    *Hierarchical setup*:\n      n_start = 32\n      max_level = min(int(log(2/n_start))+3, ceil(log(budget, 10)/4)\n    *Core loop (per level)*:\n      - Initialize h0 from parent or optimized_periodic(period)\n      - Run smooth_gradient_optimization(h0, level)\n      - Evaluate C5 safely\n    *Smoothed gradient*: use Huber loss on correlation derivatives\n    *Multi-level transition*: \n      h_next = lustre_hope(h_opt, period_change, smooth=True)\n    *Objective evaluation*: \n      corr = np.correlate(h_periodic, 1-h_periodic, mode=\"full\")\n      C5 = (1-drift) * min(corr) * dx + drift * min_period_overlap\n    *Validation*: \n      h_opt.clip(0,1), refactor_scale_to_integral(h_opt)\n\n4. **Search choices and variations**:\n    *Period schedules*: L=8,16,32,64,... or geometric sequence\n    *Adaptive restarts*: if improvement stalls, restart with new period\n    *Gradient ascent variation*: polynomial continuation with period reduction\n    *Solver variations*: external coupling with IPOPT/KNITRO\n\n5. **Compute budget and robustness**:\n    *Level time*: ~factor scale(1,n_level in 8,16,32,...)\n    *Estimated runtime*: 200-500s per level (budget sensitively depends)\n    *Termination*: level switch/iteration count/SNR threshold\n    *Fallback*: \n      base_period = 32\n      fallback(h) = louvain_transfer(h, base_period)\n\n6. **Validation and return contract**:\n  *h validation*: compute L2 distance from periodic basis\n  *Objective*: use uncertainty-aware evaluate_c5(h)\n  *Final steps*: \n    validate_periodicity(h)\n    final_std = np.std(guided_gradient(h)[-1])\n    return True if C5 goal met",
